factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 3 problems
  The reel_script says the training was 'நடத்தின' (jointly conducted) by the Tamil Nadu tribal welfare department and the Seattle India team, which matches the article, but the article's dateline and location claim 'கருமந்துறை' is correct; however the slides_spec 'யார் ஏற்பாடு?' slide lists 'குமாரபாளையம் அரசு கலை அறிவியல் கல்லூரி பேராசிரியர்' as an organiser, while the article says that professor arranged the event only (ஏற்பாடுகளை), not as an organising body alongside the department and Seattle team — this mixes two roles into one list
  The reel_script says the certificates were given by Sugandhi and Maheswaran, but the reel_script omits the key fact that the programme was held for 'உயர்கல்வி பயின்ற' (higher-educated) tribal women from Kalvarayan hills, and it omits that Jayaprakash is the Annamalai University assistant professor who chaired and coordinated the project, which is an important detail of who did what
  The caption describes the Seattle team as having 'நடத்திய' (conducted) the training alongside the department, which is consistent, but the caption's phrase 'பெரியார் பல்கலைக்கழக உள் தரக் கட்டுப்பாட்டு மைய துணை இயக்குநர் மாதேஸ்வரன்' is accurate; no invented facts found there beyond the slides-level mix-up noted above
